\s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \f1 \b0 \fs28 +\'80(NSString\'80*)\b classNameDecodedForArchiveClassName:\b0 (NSString\'80*)\i nameInArchive\
\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns the name of the class used when instantiating objects whose ostensible class, according to the archived data, is \i nameInArchive\i0 . This method returns \i nameInArchive\i0  if no substitute name has been specified using the class method (not the instance method) \b decodeClassName:asClassName:\b0 .\
\fs14\
\fs28 Note that individual instances of NSUnarchiver can each be given their own class name mappings by invoking the instance method \b decodeClassName:asClassName:\b0 . The NSUnarchiver class has no information about these instance-specific mappings, however, so they don\'27t affect the return value of this class method (that is, \b classNameDecodedForArchiveClassName:\b0 ).\
\fs14\
\pard \s58 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \b \'80classNameDecodedForArchiveClassName\f0 \fs24 :\
