\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 +\'80(void)\b decodeClassName:\b0 (NSString\'80*)\i nameInArchive \b \i0 asClassName:\b0 (NSString\'80*)\i trueName\
\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Instructs instances of NSUnarchiver to use the class named \i trueName\i0  when instantiating objects whose ostensible class, according to the archived data, is \i nameInArchive\i0 . This method enables easy conversion of unarchived data when the name of a class has changed since the archive was created.\
\fs14\
\fs28 Note that there\'27s also an instance method of the same name. An instance of NSUnarchiver can maintain its own mapping of class names. However, if both the class method and the instance method have been invoked using an identical value for \i nameInArchive\i0 , the class method takes precedence.\
\fs14\
\pard \s58 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 +\b \'80classNameDecodedForArchiveClassName:\b0 , \f3 -\f1 \b \'80decodeClassName:asClassName:\
